  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/haludaria-fasciata-the-melon-barb-formerly-barbus-fasciatus/",
      "html": "<p>A typical fish of this region is the melon barb, Haludaria (formerly Barbus or Puntius) fasciata. There are many colour strains of it in the different rivers. The most attractive varieties from an aquaristic point of view are red, but there are also yellow and orange varieties.</p><p>Wild-caught specimens can have a fantastically deep red as base colour. The males seem to glow from the inside. The melon barb becomes about 8 cm long and is completely peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/haludaria-fasciata-the-melon-barb-formerly-barbus-fasciatus/",
      "html": "<p>In the south of India rises the ancient high plateau of the Deccan, which was already formed when India was still part of Africa. From here numerous small rivers flow directly into the Indian Ocean and in many of these rivers own colour variations, subspecies or species of freshwater fish have formed due to the geographical isolation. Barbs and loaches in particular can be found here in a great variety of forms, which has not yet been scientifically researched.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/haludaria-fasciata-the-melon-barb-formerly-barbus-fasciatus/",
      "html": "<p>The water composition is secondary; the temperature should be around 26°C. A \"hibernation\" of 6-8 weeks at temperatures between 18 and 22°C has a very positive effect on the fish, but is not absolutely necessary.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/08-carp-like-fishes-2-barbs-minnows-carps-goldfish-etc/haludaria-fasciata-the-melon-barb-formerly-barbus-fasciatus/",
      "html": "<p>As a barb it nibbles on delicate plant parts if it is not sufficiently supplied with plant food.</p>"
    }
  ],
